P-I5 tags, spec 001 W1: the index CloudFront Function's component tag, for a -p branch that already holds P-I5.

The Author's prod plan (2026-11-13) refused "aws_cloudfront_function.index: tags_all lacks component": provider 6.72
tags the function, and project and environment come from prod's default_tags, so it names its component, "edge", as
the edge's other resources do. P-I5 itself is rebuilt with the same lines (its new SHA-256 in W1's note, step 5); this
delta takes infra/prod/edge.tf from the earlier P-I5 (1b830477...) to the rebuilt one, and nothing else.

Built from plain copies: edge.tf as the earlier P-I5 leaves it on a git archive export of 8e7bbd61 with P-I3, P-G1,
P-G3, P-I7, P-G4, P-G2, P-I4, P-G5, and P-6 applied, and as the rebuilt P-I5 leaves it; diff -u with a/ and b/ labels
after this preamble; never git apply. Apply it on the -p branch after P-I5's commit (and after its rebase onto W1's
tip), with `patch -p1 < <this file>` at the repository's root, and commit the result byte for byte as
"enforce(001): P-I5 tags". The earlier P-I5 plus this delta gives the rebuilt P-I5's tree, byte for byte.
--- a/infra/prod/edge.tf
+++ b/infra/prod/edge.tf
@@ -33,6 +33,10 @@
       return request;
     }
   EOT
+
+  tags = {
+    component = "edge"
+  }
 }
 
